    <h2 class="section-title">Questions Parents Ask About Our Online Tuition for Class 10</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>What is the diagnostic test and why does it cost Rs 750?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The diagnostic is a 45-minute assessment that maps your child's exact foundation gaps in Maths and Science. It covers core concepts from Classes 7 to 9 that directly affect Class 10 performance.</p><p>After the test, Swastik Sahal personally reviews the results in a 45-minute session with you and your child, providing a detailed gap analysis report and recommended study plan. The Rs 750 covers assessment design, administration, and personalised review &mdash; it ensures families who book are genuinely committed to improving.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>What subjects do you cover for CBSE Class 10?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Mathematics and Science (Physics, Chemistry, and Biology). Every topic in the NCERT Class 10 syllabus is covered &mdash; from Real Numbers and Trigonometry to Chemical Reactions and Life Processes. We also address foundation gaps from earlier classes that commonly affect Class 10 performance. Students can enrol for <strong>maths tuition</strong> only, <strong>science tuition</strong> only, or the combined programme.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>How small are the batches? Will my child get individual attention?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Batches have a maximum of 3 students (Intensive) or 5 students (Regular). This is deliberately small so Swastik can give each student real attention &mdash; identify where they are struggling in real time, adapt the pace, and ensure no one falls behind.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>Is this online only or can my child attend in person?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>We offer a hybrid model. Regular weekday classes are conducted as live <strong>online classes for Class 10 CBSE</strong> via video. Weekend sessions and diagnostic assessments can be attended in person at our Jubilee Hills centre. This gives your child online convenience with the accountability of face-to-face sessions.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>What is the class schedule?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p><strong>Regular:</strong> Monday to Saturday, 8&ndash;9 PM (6 hours per week).</p><p><strong>Intensive:</strong> Monday to Saturday, 6:30&ndash;8 PM plus Sunday test session 2&ndash;3 PM (10 hours per week).</p><p>All timings are IST, designed for students who have school during the day.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>How do you prepare students for CBSE board exams?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Our approach is diagnostic-first: we identify and fix foundation gaps before moving to board-level content. Most students struggle not because the Class 10 syllabus is hard, but because concepts from earlier classes were never properly understood.</p><p>Once gaps are fixed, board preparation becomes straightforward. We cover the full NCERT syllabus, practise board-pattern questions, and build exam technique through regular tests. This is what makes Ankuram different from generic <strong>CBSE tuition online</strong> programmes that simply rush through the syllabus.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>What if my child does not improve? Is there a refund?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The diagnostic itself gives you a clear picture before you commit to any program. If the diagnostic reveals that our approach is not the right fit, we will tell you honestly &mdash; we turn away students we cannot help.</p><p>For enrolled students, we track progress through monthly assessments. If you are not satisfied after the first month, you can discontinue month to month. We do not lock families into long-term contracts.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>What are the teacher's qualifications?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Every class is taught personally by Swastik Sahal &mdash; MSc Physics, BE Mechanical Engineering, former Amazon software engineer, with 13+ years of teaching experience across CBSE, ICSE, IB, IGCSE, and Cambridge A-Levels.</p><p>There are no teaching assistants or rotating tutors. Swastik left his tech career to focus on education full-time because he saw students being pushed through without genuine understanding.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>Why is there a fee for the diagnostic?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Because this is an actual evaluation with teacher review and feedback, not a short demo used to sell a package. It takes 90 minutes of Swastik's time. It helps us recommend the right support level instead of pushing enrolment first. If we determine Ankuram is not the right fit, we will tell you.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can my child join only for maths or only for science?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>In some cases, yes. The diagnostic helps us decide whether subject-specific <strong>online maths tuition</strong> or <strong>online science tuition for Class 10</strong> is enough, or whether a combined CBSE tuition programme is the better choice for your child's situation.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>What is the difference between the Regular and Intensive programs?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The Regular program (Rs 8,000/month) is for steady academic support through the year &mdash; 6 hours per week in a batch of 5. The Intensive program (Rs 14,000/month) is for students who need faster gap correction, closer monitoring, and stronger exam-focused intervention &mdash; 10 hours per week in a batch of 3, with Sunday test sessions.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>Is online maths tuition as effective as in-person classes?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>With batches of 3&ndash;5 students, <strong>online maths tuition</strong> at Ankuram works as well as in-person sessions. The small batch size means every student's screen is visible, every doubt gets addressed, and Swastik monitors working and approach in real time. Our hybrid model also offers weekend in-person sessions for students who want both.</p></div></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>Why should I choose Ankuram over online tuition platforms like Vedantu or Cuemath?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Online tuition platforms like Vedantu or Cuemath run 30+ student batches with rotating tutors. Ankuram provides <strong>online tuition for Class 10 CBSE</strong> in batches of 3&ndash;5 with the same teacher for every session. There is no app, no recorded content, no upsell funnel &mdash; just live teaching from a teacher with 13+ years of experience. If you are searching for the <strong>best online tuition for Class 10 CBSE</strong>, the difference is accountability and personal attention.</p></div></details>
